 "review": "Made by Claude: a new kind of lesson. The family is Emma's, from the listening lesson La famille (her parents, Thomas, Manon, aunt Julie, Léo and Chloé); the grandparents, Luc, Paul, Sophie, Hugo and Lina are invented. Check the words, the IPA and the English. No recordings yet: give a word an \"audio\" file name (in glossary_dir) and its Play button appears.",
 "intro": "A family word depends on who is speaking: the same woman is **ma mère**, **ma fille** or **ma tante**. This is the family of Emma, from the listening lesson *La famille*. Choose who « moi » is and watch every word change. Move the slider to bring in more of the family.",
 "notes": [
  "Blue words are masculine (mon), pink words are feminine (ma).",
  "Before a vowel sound, ma becomes mon: mon arrière-grand-mère, although the word is feminine.",
  "Le beau-père and la belle-mère are also the words for a stepfather and a stepmother. La belle-fille is a daughter-in-law or a stepdaughter.",
  "La femme is both the woman and the wife. Le fils /fis/: the l is silent and the s is heard. La fille is both the girl and the daughter.",
  "When a card shows no word, French has no single word for that link: people say it in full, like « le cousin de mon père »."
 ],
